    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change enforces that an invoice amount must be more than zero, across the full stack:\n\n**Server** (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/InvoicesPost.java`): tightened the validation from `amount.signum() < 0` (non-negative) to `amount.signum() <= 0` (must be positive), so a zero or negative amount is now rejected with a `400`. Updated the Javadoc to match.\n\n**Front-end** (`src/main/frontend/features/invoices/InvoiceForm.tsx`): added client-side validation \u2014 a submit with a blank, non-numeric, zero, or negative amount now sets an error and renders a `<p data-testid=\"invoice-form-amount-error\">` instead of firing the mutation, so no row is added. A valid positive amount clears the error and submits as before. The error is transient submission feedback held in `useState`, consistent with CLAUDE.md's rules.\n\nNo schema change was needed \u2014 the amount column already exists and no new persisted state is introduced, so no Flyway migration was required. Both the `@error` (rejects `0`) and `@core` (accepts `75`) specs pass.",
